### MedVault API — runnable requests
#
# Open this file in VS Code (REST Client extension), Rider, or Visual Studio and click Send Request
# on each block. Nothing here is a claim about the API: every response you see is the API answering.
#
# Start the server first:  dotnet run --project src/MedVault.Api
#
# The mock provider serves the real MedVault Demo Hospital captures, so what comes back is byte for
# byte what the hospital's API returns today. No database needed.

@host = http://localhost:5000
@mobile = 00000000
@password = medvault
@requestNb = 2026001001
@studyNb = 2604120017

### 1. Login — copy the token from the response into @token below
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/mobile/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{mobile}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "type": "P"
}

@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### 1b. Login with a wrong number — same message, same 200, on purpose
POST {{host}}/api/mobile/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "70999999",
  "password": "wrong",
  "type": "P"
}

### 2. Requests list — includes family members on the same mobile number
GET {{host}}/api/mobile/request?tcToken={{token}}

### 2b. Same call, using the Authorization header instead of the query string
GET {{host}}/api/mobile/request
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. Results for one order — 48 rows, matching the MedVault capture exactly
GET {{host}}/api/mobile/results?requestnb={{requestNb}}&tcToken={{token}}

### 3b. An order that exists but has no released results yet — 200 with an empty array, NOT a 404
GET {{host}}/api/mobile/results?requestnb=2026001002&tcToken={{token}}

### 3c. An order number that is not this patient's — 404
GET {{host}}/api/mobile/results?requestnb=9999999999&tcToken={{token}}

### 4. Radiology list — new endpoint, not in the MedVault contract
GET {{host}}/api/mobile/radiology?tcToken={{token}}

### 5. Radiology report — new endpoint
GET {{host}}/api/mobile/radiologyreport?studynb={{studyNb}}&tcToken={{token}}

### 6. File download — new endpoint. Needs Files:Root configured; returns application/pdf
GET {{host}}/api/mobile/file?path=ResultPDF/2026001001/example-report.pdf&tcToken={{token}}

### 6b. Path traversal — refused, and refused the same way a missing file is
GET {{host}}/api/mobile/file?path=../../secret.pdf&tcToken={{token}}

### 7. No token / bad token — 401
GET {{host}}/api/mobile/request?tcToken=not-a-real-token

### 8. Logout — revokes the token immediately
POST {{host}}/api/mobile/logout?tcToken={{token}}

### 8b. Re-run request 2 after logging out — now 401
GET {{host}}/api/mobile/request?tcToken={{token}}

### 9. Malformed body — 400 with the standard error shape, never a 503
POST {{host}}/api/mobile/login
Content-Type: application/json

{

### 10. Health check — no auth, for the load balancer
GET {{host}}/health
